      "downloads": 2172,
      "favourites_count": 0,
      "description": "<p>This is a compatibility patch</p>\n<p>Used to solve the bug where Echoes-of-Tarkov—Requisitions’s weapons cannot run in the realism mod environment.</p>\n<p>So you must have <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/606-spt-realism-mod/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SPT-realism mod</a> and <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/2842-echoes-of-tarkov-requisitions/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Echoes-of-Tarkov—Requisitions</a> first.</p>\n<p>After testing, it can resolve the bug of echo mod’s weapon data not loading(the detail page shows a value error of 5/90) when Echoes-of-Tarkov—Requisitions load with SPT-realism mod</p>\n<p><strong>How to install</strong></p>\n<p>Download Echo-of-Tarkov realism-compatibility.zip</p>\n<p>Drag and drop user folder into your SPT root</p>\n<p><strong>If have C:\\root folder\\user\\mods\\SPT-Realism\\db\\templates\\user_templates\\Echoes of Tarkov Requisitions: TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading ‘Templates’). Try placing the json files in the ‘‘weapons’’ folder （“user\\mods\\SPT-Realism\\db\\templates\\weapons”)</strong></p>\n",
